  "remarks": [
    "WahMan's filter is a biquad low-pass (its source): unity at DC, the resonance a peak Q times the input at the pole. Neo Filter's state-variable low-pass is the same shape away from Nyquist; the table fits the cutoff, Q and level at each Cutoff and Resonance (every 12 steps; between them, in the logarithm) so that the third octaves match within 1.5 dB.",
    "Its coefficients assume 44.1 kHz whatever the song's rate (its source): at 48 kHz its cutoff is 8.8 % higher than at 44.1 kHz. The table is fitted at 44.1 kHz.",
    "Its attribute Theviderness factor (0 by default) lowers the resonance at low cutoffs; the table assumes 0.",
    "With several tracks, each filters the input and the last one's output is what plays; the conversion reads the first track.",
